  "id": "color-temperature",
  "term": "color temperature",
  "definition": "Color temperature is a measure, expressed in kelvin, of the light appearance produced by a source and can be adjusted across a range to reproduce different daylight-like conditions. In this context, changing color temperature is relevant because it can be paired with differing circadian effects on the body.",
